steps.body:
A block can hold any statements, including another `if`. Nest one decision inside another when the second question only matters after the first is answered.

```java
if (isMember) {
    if (total >= 50) {
        shipping = 0;
    } else {
        shipping = 5;
    }
} else {
    shipping = 10;
}
```

When neither the outer `if` nor the inner one has an `else`, you can flatten them into one `if` with `&&`. These two do the same thing:

```java
if (isMember) {
    if (total >= 50) {
        System.out.println("Free shipping");
    }
}

if (isMember && total >= 50) {
    System.out.println("Free shipping");
}
```

Flat is clearer for one combined test. Nesting is clearer when each level has its own `else`. Do not flatten when the outer `if` has an `else`. In the shipping code above, `if (isMember && total >= 50)` would send a member under 50 into the outer `else`, charging 10 instead of 5.

Two gotchas:

- Always use braces. Without them, an `else` belongs to the nearest `if`, which is often not the one the indentation suggests.
- If you declare `int shipping;` before the decision, every path must assign it before you print it. Leave out an `else` and the compiler reports that `shipping` might not have been initialized.

example.code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        boolean isMember = true;
        int total = 120;
        int shipping;
        if (isMember) {
            if (total >= 50) {
                shipping = 0;
            } else {
                shipping = 5;
            }
        } else {
            if (total >= 100) {
                shipping = 0;
            } else {
                shipping = 10;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Member " + isMember + ", total " + total + ": shipping " + shipping);
        if (isMember && total >= 100) {
            System.out.println("Free gift added");
        }

        isMember = false;
        total = 30;
        if (isMember) {
            if (total >= 50) {
                shipping = 0;
            } else {
                shipping = 5;
            }
        } else {
            if (total >= 100) {
                shipping = 0;
            } else {
                shipping = 10;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Member " + isMember + ", total " + total + ": shipping " + shipping);
        if (isMember && total >= 100) {
            System.out.println("Free gift added");
        }
    }
}

